	"data": "Module 5: Search Engine — Implementation Detail\n\nPart of the Custom RAG Pipeline. See custom-rag-pipeline.md for the full system map.\n\nOverview\n\nM5 is the query-facing module — it takes a natural language query, runs dual retrieval (dense vector + BM25 sparse), and fuses results using Qdrant's server-side Reciprocal Rank Fusion. It's the brain of the pipeline: M2-M4 handle ingestion, M5 handles the question \"given this query, what's most relevant?\"\n\nSingle entry point: search(query: str, top_k:…",
